+    /**
+     * A WEB client that exists purely as a last-resort playback (stream format) fallback.
+     *
+     * <p><b>Why this is needed.</b> In the OAuth client set, the WEB/MWEB/ANDROID_VR clients are
+     * constructed with {@code ClientOptions.setPlayback(false)}. youtube-source derives
+     * {@code Client.supportsFormatLoading()} from {@code ClientOptions.getPlayback()}, and
+     * {@code YoutubeAudioTrack.process()} skips every client for which that is false. The result
+     * is that TVHTML5 ({@link Tv}) and TVHTML5_SIMPLY were the only clients that could ever
+     * resolve a stream URL, and the ytpotoken/ytvisitordata pair installed by
+     * {@code Web.setPoTokenAndVisitorData(...)} only ever influenced metadata lookups - never
+     * playback. When TVHTML5 dropped a stream mid-track and TVHTML5_SIMPLY hit "Sign in to
+     * confirm you're not a bot", the track was dropped with AllClientsFailedException.
+     *
+     * <p><b>Why a separate instance.</b> The playback flag is per-{@code ClientOptions}, so the
+     * metadata-only WEB instance cannot also serve playback. This instance keeps playback enabled
+     * and is placed <em>last</em> in the client array, so the existing TVHTML5-first ordering is
+     * untouched and this only ever runs as a recovery attempt.
+     *
+     * <p><b>Why canHandleRequest is false.</b> Mirrors {@link Tv}: returning false keeps this
+     * client out of {@code YoutubeAudioSourceManager.loadItem()} entirely, so track/playlist/mix
+     * resolution behaviour is byte-for-byte identical to before. Only the playback loop, which
+     * ignores canHandleRequest and looks solely at supportsFormatLoading(), can reach it.
+     */
+    private static final class WebPlaybackFallback extends WebWithThumbnail
+    {
+        @Override
+        public boolean canHandleRequest(String identifier)
+        {
+            return false;
+        }
+    }
 }
